# API Versioning (`/api/v1`)

Detail: `docs/api/conventions.md` · Skill: `lancehive-conventions`

## Config

- `config/api.php` — `route_version`, `prefix` (`api/v1`), `features_routes` (`routes/features/v1`)
- `.env` — `API_ROUTE_VERSION=v1` (URL segment; distinct from OpenAPI `API_VERSION` semver)

## Folder rules (what gets versioned)

| Versioned | Not versioned |
|-----------|---------------|
| `routes/features/v1/*.php` | `app/Features/{Feature}/` (models, actions, services) |
| URL prefix `/api/v1` | `database/migrations`, factories, seeders |
| Scramble `api_path` | `tests/Feature/{Feature}/` — use `$this->apiUrl()` |

**Do not** add `V1/` subfolders under `app/Features/` while only one API version exists.

## Routes

```php
// routes/api.php
Route::prefix(config('api.route_version'))->group(function (): void {
    require config('api.features_routes').'/auth.php';
    // require config('api.features_routes').'/delivery.php';
});
```

New feature route file → `routes/features/v1/{feature}.php`.

## Tests

`$this->apiUrl('login')` → `/api/v1/login`. Never hardcode `/api/` without version.

## v2 later

Add `routes/features/v2/` + second prefix group in `routes/api.php`. Duplicate controllers only when HTTP contract breaks. Freeze v1 files.
